<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lorsch Codex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1170–<a href="/years/1195">1195</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Codex Laureshamensis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorsch">Lorsch</a> Codex is a cartulary compiled at Lorsch Abbey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> in the late 12th century, recording the abbey's history and copies of thousands of charters of donation from the 8th century onwards. It contains the earliest written mention of hundreds of places in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and is a major source for Carolingian society and landholding. It is kept in the Bavarian State Archives in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lorsch-codex.jpg" alt="Lorsch Codex" width="200" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_Laureshamensis_Initial-D.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
